     <property name="text">
      <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Road Details - Center Line Creation Help&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Road Details function linearizes road polygons to center lines. This is particularly useful for creating road networks from area data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Required Inputs&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Usage Layer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Polygon layer with road surfaces or transportation routes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Should contain polygons representing roads, paths or other linear infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically ALKIS data with usage type "traffic area" or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buffer Distance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distance in meters for internal buffering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Default: 2.0 meters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Smaller values for narrow paths, larger for wide roads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Affects the accuracy of centerline creation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Processing Algorithm&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The tool uses various methods for centerline creation:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inward Buffer:&lt;/strong&gt; Creates an inward buffer to approximate the medial axis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skeleton Extraction:&lt;/strong&gt; Extracts the "skeleton" of the polygon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fallback Method:&lt;/strong&gt; For complex geometries, a centroid-based line is created&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clipping:&lt;/strong&gt; The resulting line is clipped to the original polygon boundary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Parameter Settings&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buffer Distance Recommendations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Footpaths:&lt;/strong&gt; 0.5 - 1.0 meters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secondary roads:&lt;/strong&gt; 1.5 - 3.0 meters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main roads:&lt;/strong&gt; 3.0 - 6.0 meters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highways:&lt;/strong&gt; 5.0 - 10.0 meters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Output Properties&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geometry:&lt;/strong&gt; LineString (line data)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes:&lt;/strong&gt; All original attributes from the input layer are transferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate System:&lt;/strong&gt; Identical to the input layer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Use Cases&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Converting ALKIS traffic areas to road networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating routing networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simplifying complex traffic area geometries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparation for network analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Tips and Notes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test different buffer distances for optimal results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very complex or narrow polygons may lead to unexpected results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The tool works best with relatively simple, elongated road polygons&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For incorrect results, data cleaning or different buffer values may help&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
